[Event "London casual game"]
[Site "London ENG"]
[Date "1851.06.21"]
[Round "?"]
[White "Anderssen, Adolf"]
[Black "Kieseritzky, Lionel"]
[Result "1-0"]

{The "Immortal Game". White gives away a bishop, both rooks and the queen,
then mates with the three minor pieces left.} 1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Bc4 Qh4+
4. Kf1 b5 5. Bxb5 Nf6 6. Nf3 Qh6 7. d3 Nh5 8. Nh4 Qg5 9. Nf5 c6 10. g4 Nf6 11.
Rg1 cxb5 12. h4 Qg6 13. h5 Qg5 14. Qf3 Ng8 15. Bxf4 Qf6 16. Nc3 Bc5 17. Nd5
Qxb2 18. Bd6 $1 {Both rooks are left hanging.} 18... Bxg1 $2 (18... Qxa1+ {first,
with check, was better.}) 19. e5 Qxa1+ 20. Ke2 Na6 21. Nxg7+ Kd8 22.
Qf6+ $3 Nxf6 23. Be7# {[%csl Rd8][%cal Ge7d8]} 1-0

