[White "Morphy, Paul"]
[Black "Duke Karl / Count Isouard"]
[Result "1-0"]

{The "Opera Game", played during a performance at the Paris opera.} 1. e4 e5 2.
Nf3 d6 3. d4 Bg4 $6 4. dxe5 Bxf3 5. Qxf3 dxe5 6. Bc4 Nf6 7. Qb3 {Two threats:
Bxf7+ and Qxb7.} 7... Qe7 8. Nc3 c6 9. Bg5 b5 10. Nxb5 $1 {White gives a piece
to keep the lines open.} 10... cxb5 11. Bxb5+ Nbd7 12. O-O-O Rd8 13. Rxd7 $1
Rxd7 14. Rd1 Qe6 15. Bxd7+ Nxd7 16. Qb8+ $3 {[%cal Gb3b8,Gd1d8]} 16... Nxb8 17.
Rd8# {Black's bishop on f8 and rook on h8 never moved.} 1-0

